{"authored" [{"question" "q-31397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{x{log}_{3}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0fe9e8494485603aa2f1a0d0e2a29d59ad83a7b6f14b22479a6b3e533506f8e" "basis" 1138 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={log}_{3}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{x{log}_{3}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{log}_{3}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0fe9e8494485603aa2f1a0d0e2a29d59ad83a7b6f14b22479a6b3e533506f8e" "basis" 1138 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "222fe31908a93b53786ab4aa511ab10b01045386db1a176ffaba2a0d129ce6d5" "basis" 1138 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/que